# What Vercel is allowed to see, which is the tracker and nothing else.
#
# Only the front end in web/ is deployable: the collector is a Python process
# that holds Broadcastify credentials and listens to a scanner, and a
# datacentre is the wrong place for both. The hosted half of the tracker is
# three functions in web/api/ that never reach back here -- the radio machine
# pushes to them.
#
# Written as a denylist of everything with web/ carved back out, rather than a
# list of things to leave behind, because the failure that matters is the one
# nobody thought to name. A .env with a live push token in it is exactly the
# file an ignore list forgets, and this way it is never a question.
#
# Vercel reads this relative to the project's Root Directory. Set that to `web`
# -- which is the documented setup -- and this file is not consulted at all; it
# is here for `vercel deploy` run from the repository root, where without it the
# whole tree goes up.
/*
!/web

# And the two things inside web/ that are made, not written.
/web/node_modules
/web/dist
